#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Sample bitstrings from the Krylov circuits {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "6. Bitstrings aus den Krylov-Circuits sampeln {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, you would run the transpiled circuits and measure. This is the noiseless (statevector) version of that step, showing the bitstrings SKQD would collect. Simulate each untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and sample the resulting statevector with [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"
msgstr "Auf Hardware würdest du die transpilierten Circuits ausführen und messen. Dies ist die rauschfreie (Statevector-)Version dieses Schritts, die die Bitstrings zeigt, die SKQD sammeln würde. Simuliere jeden nicht transpilierten [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") mit [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") und sample den resultierenden Statevector mit [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate is validate-then-rotate under simulation (it checks that the incoming state occupies its reference determinant, then applies the rotation). Therefore, the input is the plain occupation determinant: the lowest `nocc` modes filled per spin, with no rotation. The gate applies `reference_rotation` itself.\n"
msgstr "Ein [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\")-Gate validiert in der Simulation zuerst und rotiert dann (es prüft, dass der eingehende Zustand seine Referenzdeterminante besetzt, und wendet dann die Rotation an). Daher ist die Eingabe die einfache Besetzungsdeterminante: die niedrigsten `nocc` Moden pro Spin gefüllt, ohne Rotation. Das Gate wendet `reference_rotation` selbst an.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooling the samples from all five Krylov circuits, the support is tiny: a few hundred distinct bitstrings out of the $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ determinants in the `(4, 4)` sector. This concentration, a direct consequence of the momentum-basis sparsity established in step 2, makes the subsequent classical diagonalization tractable.\n"
msgstr "Fasst man die Samples aus allen fünf Krylov-Circuits zusammen, ist der Träger winzig: einige hundert verschiedene Bitstrings aus den $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ Determinanten im Sektor `(4, 4)`. Diese Konzentration, eine direkte Folge der in Schritt 2 festgestellten Dünnbesetztheit in der Impulsbasis, macht die anschließende klassische Diagonalisierung handhabbar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plotting the counts with [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) makes the sparsity visible. A few configurations dominate, led by the reference determinant.\n"
msgstr "Das Darstellen der Counts mit [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) macht die Sparsity sichtbar. Wenige Konfigurationen dominieren, angeführt von der Referenzdeterminante.\n"

